    {
      "id": 6,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Data Source and Request Flow",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 13
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Provider:** Kraken public REST market-data API. No API key or account is required.\\n\\n**Ingestion:** A dedicated market-data worker polls the configured pair every 60 seconds by default. It persists successful snapshots and worker status to PostgreSQL. A database advisory lock prevents overlapping pollers.\\n\\n**API routes:** GET /v1/market/kraken/tickers lists tracked pairs; GET /v1/market/kraken/ticker returns the configured pair; GET /v1/market/kraken/history?pair=XBTUSD&range=24h&limit=500 returns a chronological, downsampled series; GET /v1/market/kraken/summary?pair=XBTUSD&range=24h calculates price movement and range statistics; GET /v1/market/kraken/status reports worker health. Supported ranges are 1h, 24h, and 7d.\\n\\n**Trace:** Find the kraken.public_ticker span in Tempo under service market-data-worker. fetched_at is when Kaviont retrieved the snapshot, not an exchange event timestamp. The integration reads public market data only and does not submit orders."
      }
    }
